sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Dürer/Camper facial grids — whole-grid deformation test on human profile landmarks (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 67.3/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Dense Camper-frame fits on 12 ordered pairs: median RMSE null 0.083 -> Dürer 0.069 (LOO 0.092 vs null LOO 0.091) -> affine 0.052; median R_Dürer 0.45 (range 0.01-0.73); noise floor 0.003 so the Dürer residual is 24x noise; fitted c 0.07-1.57, k -0.68..+0.57 against Dürer's own |k| ~ 0.15. E5: r(k, dtan E-line) = 0.62, p = 0.033, slope 0.48. KS null vs Dürer p = 0.10. Controls: exact Dürer grid recovered to 1.8e-15; scrambled correspondences 0.160 (> real 0.069); nose-only ablation on an exact grid leaves 0.015 (> 0). omega sweep: E-line inclination strictly monotone in omega (Lean camper_facial_angle_index); convexity 8.5 deg (n = 2, norm 12 +/- 4), nasolabial 93 +/- 39 deg (n = 4, columella still misdetected on two faces). Verdict: mixed — strong form not supported, bounded form supported. Overall 67.3/100 (faithfulness 63.8, reproducibility 75.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 22ee087d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 45, Parameter expressivity 72, Morphometric validation 68, Source and data traceability 82, Code-to-model traceability 76, Reproducibility package 70. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_040_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py at 22ee087d, image/png, 608335 B, 1700×1500 px, artifact_sha256 fe2b61061643bce37151c4a4aad81a6a010df2bd3ba096ab8d1dbd8598e5a74a (sha256 fe2b61061643bce37151c4a4aad81a6a010df2bd3ba096ab8d1dbd8598e5a74a), spec_fingerprint 814bd4703a2eb758261f2f135d1296d3536158edeb11b7060849c7f375a95447. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 814bd4703a2eb758261f2f135d1296d3536158edeb11b7060849c7f375a95447; artifact_sha256: fe2b61061643bce37151c4a4aad81a6a010df2bd3ba096ab8d1dbd8598e5a74a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/paper_citations.bib=1279402c7d3411df..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/scout_manifest.json=c738aa8c422f8f96..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/beverly_sills_profile.jpg=679a08ff1f459089..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/helen_keller_1904_profile.jpg=7fa2a48b647c3b09..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/kubra_gumusay_2023_profile.jpg=aaa06c6f5c336da7..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/margaret_of_hesse_profile.jpg=1b38e84fc0eb1594..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/nasta_rojc_profile.jpg=4b5ed492fb19ec93..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/nell_walden_1905_profile.png=b1f49c57c7aeefee..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/roberts_2013_profile.jpg=643f14a150df84e0..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/romy_schneider_profile.jpg=0857743562b65c3a..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/winifred_odunoku_profile.jpg=b48ece4b38e69468..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/t1917_040_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_reference.json=73476821074c4716..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/thompson_1917_pages/ongrowthform1917thom_leaf759_p740.jpg=9e583cdcbd5c7ced..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/thompson_1917_pages/ongrowthform1917thom_leaf761_p742.jpg=214db8a09bd3fdfe...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-040-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Dürer heads redrawn in rectangular (Fig. 364) and oblique (Fig. 366) nets; Hough digitisation of the pinned scan gives omega = 81 / 99 deg, i.e. |k| ~ 0.15 | Camper's facial angle 'is the index to a general deformation' (p. 742 footnote); no measurements in the source; reconstructed_in_script: E1 stretch, E3 shear with k = -cot(omega), E4 affine, E5 tan(phi') = tan(phi) + k; Dürer sub-family fit (5 dof) in the Camper frame vs scale+shift null and affine bound | 12 ordered pairs of 4 accepted photographs, landmark-only and dense (30 semilandmarks) configurations, LOO-CV, noise floor, controls; transfer_boundary: 2-D soft-tissue silhouettes from photographs, not skulls or 3-D form; Commons photographs are an analogue of Camper's drawn series and are labelled as such | the Camper horizontal is approximated by the photograph horizontal after a declared deskew; +/-5 deg pose perturbation moves median R_Dürer 0.45 -> 0.37-0.40; does_not_claim: anything about populations or 'types' | growth or developmental mechanism." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor (different provider) — still builder-scored'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R10', 'item': 'Implement E2 (logarithmic stretch) and compare the three Thompson families on the same pairs'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R11', 'item': 'Update the KG yaml code loci to the Pass-2 line ranges and add fit_durer / controls as explicit loci'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R8b', 'item': 'Edge-assisted or learned segmentation to rescue gradient / halftone / textured backgrounds (Keller, Walden, Sills, Gümüşay) and reach n >= 10 faces; manual-landmark cross-check to turn the re-detection floor into a true landmark-uncertainty floor'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R9', 'item': 'Fix the Camper horizontal anatomically (tragus/porion detection) instead of the photograph horizontal, so the shear/rotation split does not depend on the declared deskew'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.673"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (builder-assessor, single-agent Pass 2; second assessor pending R1)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 .
}

